# Begin with the End in Mind -Final Project Overview

## Multi-page web application
#### In the final project, students take on the role of web designers to create a multi-page digital magazine for a fictional user or community.

#### They identify their target audience and brand, plan the layout for key pages like a home page and article page, and then use AI in Guide mode to help them generate the HTML and CSS needed to build their site. 

---

### **When Project Begins:** Final lesson of the unit

### The project extends over three class periods. Beginning in Lesson 13.

## Sample

#### In this example, the student designed a web app to showcase local events and activities in their town.

<img src="https://images.code.org/0fa53a5cbf5480e4c10f9f2bc406506f-image-1765910932701.png" alt="Sample student project of a website giving informaiton about events happening locally in their community" width="850px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">

---

## Primary Concepts Practiced
####✅ User-centered design
####✅ Wireframing and decomposition
####✅ Brand identity
####✅ Accessibility and responsiveness
#### ✅Prompt engineering and evaluating AI output


## Project criteria used for evaluation

#### This project lets students apply their design and coding skills in a creative, authentic way while learning how AI can support the web development process.

